Always build and use the STL interface (TIXML_USE_STL)

TIXML_USE_STL changes the layout of TiXmlString-holding classes (std::string
instead of TinyXML's own TiXmlString) and adds std::string/iostream methods.
The shared library is compiled with it, so a program that includes
tinyxml.h without -DTIXML_USE_STL would use a different class layout than
the library it links. The header now defines it itself, as the
distributions' libtinyxml packages do.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate (packaging: upstream ships no library build)

--- a/tinyxml.h	2011-05-15 11:24:57.000000000 +0900
+++ b/tinyxml.h	2026-11-01 12:51:14.618435590 +0900
@@ -43,6 +43,12 @@
 #define DEBUG
 #endif
 
+/* This build of the library is compiled with the STL interface; every
+   user must see the same class layout. */
+#ifndef TIXML_USE_STL
+#define TIXML_USE_STL
+#endif
+
 #ifdef TIXML_USE_STL
 	#include <string>
  	#include <iostream>
